<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zalmoxis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zalmoxis was a god or deified teacher of the Getae and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacians">Dacians</a> north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> reports that the Getae believed they did not die but went to Zalmoxis, and that every four years they sent him a messenger by throwing a man onto spears. Greek writers also told of him as a former slave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythagoras">Pythagoras</a>, a story Herodotus himself doubted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zalmoxis.jpg" alt="Zalmoxis" width="151" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zalmoxis_Aleksandrovo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
